% A dot before a tie or a slur, as in C.-C or .(E G), draws it dotted
% (section 4.11 of the abc standard) and plays it like a plain one.
% parsemusic() (parseabc.c) read the dot of a dotted tie as a staccato
% and reported a "Malformed note" on the - that follows it (GitHub issue
% #80).  Tune 2 is tune 1 with plain ties and slurs: abc2midi plays both
% alike.
X:1
T:Dotted ties and slurs
C:abc2midi test
M:C
L:1/4
Q:1/4=120
K:C
C.-C .(E G) | [CE].-[CE] c.-c- | c A.-A2 |]

X:2
T:Plain ties and slurs
C:abc2midi test
M:C
L:1/4
Q:1/4=120
K:C
C-C (E G) | [CE]-[CE] c-c- | c A-A2 |]
